<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-tŭmŭlo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To heap up like a mound</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ovis stragulum molle pulvere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 33, 51, § 100</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To furnish with a mound, to inter, bury</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saucium ingestā humo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					460</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 3, 3, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 8,
				57, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>